          "title": "Show HN: Koi.rest – watch some fish and regain your balance",
          "url": "https://koi.rest",
          "source": "Hacker News",
          "date": "2026-09-24T21:33:03Z",
          "language": "en",
          "section": "us_news",
          "raw_content": "Hi there. My name is Paul. I’m a developer, an explorer and I’ve got ADHD. As of the beginning of August, I’m also unemployed. This last part, along with everything else this past year, has caused me a great deal of stress. While our balcony zen garden project is yet to be completed, I had an idea to create a virtual one that everyone can use. It's an idea that, unfortunately, I’ve been postponing for a while now, mostly because I have no fucking idea how to do it as I don’t know JavaScript, and I don't have the capacity to learn it right now. So I let perfect be the enemy of good and, well... just kept the idea to myself. Then I said \"fuck it\" and used AI to make the thing I really wanted to make. I realized I didn't want \"perfect\". I wanted \"good enough\". I tweaked, added, removed, drew, researched, questioned, tested... I just wasn't the one coding it. So now, instead of occupying my ",
